====================================================================================================
K.  SENSITIVITY / POSITIVE CONTROL: inject a known density modulation above tau=1
    into the REAL zeta tape and check the pipeline recovers it at the predicted size.
    A density ripple  rho -> 1 + A cos(2 pi tau0 u)  displaces u_k by  -(A/(2 pi tau0)) sin(2 pi tau0 u_k)
    and produces a line of height K = A^2 U / 4  at tau0.  Target bin excess is over a
    0.05 bin containing that line: dK_bin = (A^2 U/4)/(U*0.05) = A^2/0.2.
====================================================================================================
  T=1e+06  U=4001  tau0=1.6
          A  pred dK_bin  meas dK_bin    sigma       z  K(tau0) meas     pred
       0.05       0.0125       0.0042   0.0658    0.06          2.21     2.50
       0.10       0.0500       0.0141   0.0664    0.21          7.58    10.00
       0.20       0.2000       0.0500   0.0689    0.73         32.72    40.01
       0.40       0.8000       0.1827   0.0780    2.34        136.88   160.06
       0.80       3.2000       0.6263   0.1085    5.77        505.52   640.24
  => the pipeline is NOT blind above tau=1; it detects a ripple of amplitude A at the
     predicted amplitude.  The 3-sigma floor corresponds to A ~ sqrt(0.2*3*sigma).

